# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in every working tree, on
# every platform. See CLAUDE.md, "Source encoding and format strings".
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turns every source
# file CRLF, and the tests that read source as text and match across a line
# break fail on code that is correct. BitWiringTest and
# UntrackCoolingOffWiringTest did exactly that on the owner's machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF to run. Left exactly as committed (gradlew.bat
# already is CRLF), so this file does not force a renormalization of it.
*.bat -text

# Byte for byte.
*.jar binary
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.p12 binary
